# The PyPI wheels the bindings probe compares with (scripts/native/test-bindings.sh): the same versions as the ones
# built from sdist (pins.conf), pinned by sha256 so a baseline cannot change under the probe. They are evidence only and
# never shipped. netCDF4 is 1.7.5, not the pinned 1.7.5.1: 1.7.5.1 has no binary wheel on PyPI for either architecture.
# Locked per architecture with hashes (--no-deps: the bindings' dependencies come from the test environment's lock):
#   uv pip compile --no-deps --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --python-platform <arch>-manylinux_2_28 \
#     scripts/native/baseline-requirements.in -o scripts/native/baseline-requirements-<arch>.txt
